@@ -0,0 +1,54 @@
+# Experimental LXR tonal-drum kernel port
+
+Upstream: https://github.com/erica-synths/lxr-desktop-app
+Revision: a43cd4fcda23ec3d577dc425261c3eb28bd5abff.
+Copyright (C) 2012-2026 Erica Synths. GPL-3.0-only with the additional permission
+and terms in the unmodified NOTICE.md, copied alongside the unmodified LICENSE.
+This modified implementation is Delxr, not official Erica Synths firmware.
+The firmware UI must identify the modified version; preserving this notice alone
+is not a substitute for that UI requirement.
+
+This is a restricted adaptation of the tonal drum kernel, not a full LXR voice
+or a bit-exact port of an LXR preset:
+
+- `sine_table.inc` is the exact 4,097 values of `sine_table` in
+  `Core/Src/Soundengine/DSPAudio/wavetable.c`.
+- Table addressing, linear interpolation, oscillator trigger phase and sine phase
+  modulation scale follow `Oscillator.c` (`calcSine`, `calcFmSineBlock`) and
+  `DrumVoice.c` (`Drum_trigger`, async/sync paths).
+- Rational envelope shape `(1+k)*x/(1+k*abs(x))` and linear envelope progression
+  follow `Decay.c` and `SlopeEg2.c`. Snap's `24*x*x` and 0.2 decrement follow
+  `snapEg.c`. The amp's sample-rate 0.1 smoothing follows the original amp filter.
+- Envelope targets run every 64 samples as the checked upstream configuration
+  does. Upstream's actual `REAL_FS` is 44,140 Hz; Delxr uses 44,100 Hz.
+- Parameters use Hz, seconds and normalized amounts. Amp slope (-.85), pitch
+  slope (-.9), pitch duration (45 ms), snap timing/amount scaling and modulator
+  ratio (1.5) are chosen prototype settings. They are not asserted equivalent to
+  any stored LXR preset or the full manual parameter mappings.
+- Pitch modulation follows the LXR additive multiplier structure, including its
+  envelope-dependent FM amount. The amplitude uses a decay-only restriction of
+  the LXR attack/decay envelope. Trigger always resets phase and envelope state;
+  the upstream conditional phase reset and retrigger-over-existing-tail policy
+  are not reproduced.
+- Waveforms other than sine, envelope attack/repeat and adjustable slope,
+  transient samples/offset mode, oscillator mixing, noise, SVF, drive, dither,
+  bit reduction, LFO, velocity routing matrix, hardware faders, sequencer, morph,
+  FX and other engine architectures are not ported here. Existing Deluge amp,
+  filter, effects and sequencer remain separate integration stages.
+- State is per `KickVoice` instance with no heap allocation or global voice
+  array. Frequency and parameters are latched at trigger. Output peak is about
+  2^28, leaving headroom before the existing Deluge amplitude/pan/filter path.
+- Defensive finite/clamp checks, alias-risk frequency bounds and well-defined
+  signed phase modulation conversion are Delxr additions. The source's FM is
+  not band-limited; this port does not claim alias-free metallic sounds.
+
+Host behavioral check: `tests/lxr-kick.cpp` in the Delxr repository (outside the
+firmware source glob). From the Delxr root:
+
+```sh
+g++ -std=c++23 -O2 -Wall -Wextra -Werror \
+  -Iupstream/firmware/src/deluge/dsp/lxr \
+  upstream/firmware/src/deluge/dsp/lxr/kick.cpp tests/lxr-kick.cpp \
+  -o /tmp/test-lxr-kick
+/tmp/test-lxr-kick
+```
